  1	# Exposed UI
  2	
  3	Import components and public types from the `src/lib/ui/index.ts` barrel (for example `./lib/ui` from `src/Example.svelte`). Load `../lib/ui/styles.css` once in `src/routes/+layout.svelte`. It includes tokens, actions, patterns, focus rings, hidden captions, highlighted text and animation prerequisites. Field and Notice keep scoped styles. `/design-system` is the interactive reference in development only and requires no declarations API. Production returns 404 and hides its footer link.
  4	
  5	Features own amounts, availability, chart geometry, URLs, analytics and async work. UI accepts formatted strings and presentation models. Pages own grids and section spacing. Use the [composition recipes](COMPOSITION.md) for native rows, declarations and identities.
  6	
  7	| Component                              | Contract                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
  8	| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
  9	| Button, ButtonLink                     | `variant` primary/secondary/quiet/subtle; `size` regular/large/compact/inline. Native attributes and handlers pass through. Button defaults to `type="button"`; links require `href`.                                                |
 10	| Field                                  | Required visible `label`; `type` text/search/date/email; bindable string `value`; `defaultValue` supports native reset. `hint` and `error` join caller `aria-describedby`. Native attributes reach the input; `class` reaches the wrapper. |
 11	| Textarea | Required visible `label`; bindable string `value`; `defaultValue` supports native reset. `hint` and `error` join caller `aria-describedby`. Native textarea attributes pass through; `class` reaches the wrapper. Resizes vertically. |
 12	| SearchField                            | Required `label`, `help` snippet and `onclear`; bindable string `value` and native `input` reference; optional `shortcut`. Native attributes including `class` reach the input. Caller owns query behavior and focus restoration.    |
 13	| Notice                                 | `tone` neutral/accent/warning. Native div attributes pass through. Caller chooses announcement `role`.                                                                                                                               |
 14	| Badge                                  | `variant` result (default), profile or legend. `class` adds a root hook without replacing appearance.                                                                                                                                |
 15	| MessageState                           | Required `title`; `variant` centered (default) or detail; `level` 1/2 changes semantics independently of appearance. Optional `icon`, `children`, `actions`, `role`, additive root `class`.                                          |
 16	| SectionHeading                         | Required `id`, `title`; optional `level` 1/2/3 and trailing children. Heading presentation stays independent of rank.                                                                                                                |
 17	| Disclosure                             | Required `summary`, children; `variant` names (default) or plain. Native details attributes, additive root `class`, bindable `open`.                                                                                                 |
 18	| Metric                                 | Required `label`, formatted `value`; optional `regionLabel`, `available`, `description`, `level` 2/3. `variant` default or expanded; optional `align` start/end overrides variant and responsive text alignment. Available values remain keyboard-scrollable regions; unavailable text remains ordinary text.    |
 19	| DeclarationCard                        | Required `heading`, `registered`, children snippets. `variant` default or compact changes padding.                                                                                                                                   |
 20	| ValueRow                               | Required `source` and `value` snippets. Owns its `li` layout, including outside `.funding-list`; nested lists retain native layout.                                                                                                  |
 21	| DataTable                              | Required text `caption`, `head` snippet and body children. Callers supply native rows, cells, scope and column-specific classes. No numeric alignment or column widths are assumed.                                                  |
 22	| IdentityHeader                         | Required `name`, `kind`, `metadata`; optional `values`, `navigation`, `level` 1/2/3.                                                                                                                                                 |
 23	| ResultRow, DeclarationList             | Native `li` and `ol` wrappers; children and optional accessible `label`. ResultRow callers supply their own anchor and may add a root `class` for a local palette.                                                                   |
 24	| SignedBarList                          | `bars: SignedBar[]`, `baseline`; `variant` default or compact. Values are formatted strings; widths and signs come from features.                                                                                                    |
 25	| BarChart, PieChart                     | Typed `ChartBar[]` geometry and `PieSlice[]` presentation data. Features calculate shares, signs and totals. See [RegistrationTimeline](../../RegistrationTimeline.svelte) and [FunderSummary](../../FunderSummary.svelte).          |
 26	| ViewLinks, ViewLink, Pagination        | Native navigation. Callers own destinations/current page; Pagination owns bound availability.                                                                                                                                        |
 27	| Icon, IconIndicator                    | Canonical `IconName`; Icon is decorative. IconIndicator owns focus, pointer and Escape hints.                                                                                                                                        |
 28	| HighlightedText, Spinner, SkeletonRows | Literal text highlights and decorative progress.                                                                                                                                                                                     |
 29	
 30	The first DataTable body row has a top divider, including when callers visually hide column headings.
 31	
 32	Classes on native-attribute components accept Svelte class arrays and objects. Where a structural component exposes `class`, it adds a root hook. No class replacement API is supported. Use finite variants for existing appearances; caller-authored snippet classes own feature text and arrangements. The recipes show those classes explicitly.
 33	
 34	Tokens in [tokens.css](tokens.css) own colors, spacing, type and focus. Override `--accent` on a container for another palette, such as `var(--accent-funder)`. The Exposed wordmark stays white across entity contexts. The landing heading uses member purple for MPs and funder teal for financial interests. Entity indicators, badges, highlights, charts and declared values derive their colors from the local accent; a ResultRow root `class` can select that palette explicitly. Actions use neutral `--action`, `--action-ink`, `--action-border`, `--action-surface` and `--action-hover`; all focus rings use `--focus-color`, independently of entity palettes. Keep action and focus tokens neutral in member and funder containers. `--focus-width` and `--focus-offset` apply at the root or on a container. Native links, buttons and summaries add one pixel to the offset. Do not import internal stylesheets individually.
 35	
 36	The [barrel](index.ts) is the public inventory. The gallery covers native disclosure/input behavior, precise metric overflow, repeated association IDs and pointer tooltip lifecycle. Financial parsing and availability decisions belong in feature adapters, never in UI components.
 37	
 38	UI-owned snippet classes are `.results-list` (list reset and divider), `.entity-text` (shrinkable content), `.entity-name` (result anchor typography and hover), `.entity-alias` (secondary result text), `.funding-list` (nested list reset and spacing), `.declaration-reference`, `.payment-type`, `.currency-label`, `.empty-entry` (declaration context), `.amount` (exact value typography), and `.entry-count`/`.partial-note` (secondary chart/table text). These work with the single UI stylesheet import. Feature grids and custom table columns stay in callers.
